IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc8-part7-lotteries`

-- ccc8-tests-part7-lotteries.l4 -- tests for ccc8-part7-lotteries.l4 (sections 206, 207, 207.1, 209, 213). Expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- The stand-in below is NOT the penalty of section 787(1) (outside this part): it states nothing, so only the limb of this part is tested.
`s 206(1) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 206 -- lotteries and games of chance`

-- (1) "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... or ... summary conviction who (a) ... (j)": all ten paragraphs create the offence
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD `s 206(1) the person commits the offence` a EQUALS JUST TRUE) (LIST `s 206(1)(a) makes, prints, advertises or publishes, or causes or procures to be made, printed, advertised or published, any proposal, scheme or plan for disposing of any property by lots, cards, tickets or any mode of chance whatever`, `s 206(1)(b) sells, barters, exchanges or otherwise disposes of, or causes or procures, or aids or assists in, the sale, barter, exchange or other disposal of, or offers for sale, barter or exchange, any lot, card, ticket or other means or device for disposing of any property by lots, tickets or any mode of chance whatever`, `s 206(1)(c) knowingly sends, transmits, mails, ships, delivers or allows to be sent, transmitted, mailed, shipped or delivered, or knowingly accepts for carriage or transport or conveys any article that is used or intended for use in carrying out any such device, proposal, scheme or plan`, `s 206(1)(d) conducts or manages any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind for the purpose of determining who, or the holders of what lots, tickets, numbers or chances, are the winners of any property so proposed to be disposed of`, `s 206(1)(e) conducts, manages or is a party to any scheme, contrivance or operation of any kind by which any person, on payment of any sum of money, or the giving of any valuable security, shall become entitled to receive a larger sum of money or amount of valuable security than the sum or amount paid or given, by reason of the fact that other persons have paid or given`, `s 206(1)(f) disposes of any goods, wares or merchandise by any game of chance or any game of mixed chance and skill in which the contestant or competitor pays money or other valuable consideration`, `s 206(1)(g) induces any person to stake or hazard any money or other valuable property or thing on the result of any dice game, three-card monte, punch board, coin table or on the operation of a wheel of fortune`, `s 206(1)(h) for valuable consideration carries on or plays or offers to carry on or to play, or employs any person to carry on or play in a public place or a place to which the public have access, the game of three-card monte`, `s 206(1)(i) receives bets of any kind on the outcome of a game of three-card monte`, `s 206(1)(j) being the owner of a place, permits any person to play the game of three-card monte therein`)
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the punishment` `s 206(1) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 206(1) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- (2) "three-card monte means the game commonly known as three-card monte and includes any other game that is similar to it"
#ASSERT `s 206(2) three-card monte` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(2) three-card monte` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(2) three-card monte` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3.1) "fair or exhibition means an event where agricultural or fishing products are presented or where activities relating to agriculture or fishing take place"
#ASSERT `s 206(3.1) fair or exhibition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(3.1) fair or exhibition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(3.1) fair or exhibition` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) "Paragraphs (1)(f) and (g), in so far as they do not relate to a dice game, three-card monte, punch board or coin table, do not apply to the board of an annual fair or exhibition, or to any operator of a concession leased by that board within its own grounds and operated during the fair or exhibition on those grounds"
--                                                                                       act                       dice etc board operator on grounds
#ASSERT `s 206(3) paragraphs (1)(f) and (g) do not apply to the person` `s 206(1)(f) disposes of any goods, wares or merchandise by any game of chance or any game of mixed chance and skill in which the contestant or competitor pays money or other valuable consideration` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(3) paragraphs (1)(f) and (g) do not apply to the person` `s 206(1)(g) induces any person to stake or hazard any money or other valuable property or thing on the result of any dice game, three-card monte, punch board, coin table or on the operation of a wheel of fortune` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(3) paragraphs (1)(f) and (g) do not apply to the person` `s 206(1)(g) induces any person to stake or hazard any money or other valuable property or thing on the result of any dice game, three-card monte, punch board, coin table or on the operation of a wheel of fortune` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(3) paragraphs (1)(f) and (g) do not apply to the person` `s 206(1)(f) disposes of any goods, wares or merchandise by any game of chance or any game of mixed chance and skill in which the contestant or competitor pays money or other valuable consideration` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(3) paragraphs (1)(f) and (g) do not apply to the person` `s 206(1)(i) receives bets of any kind on the outcome of a game of three-card monte` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) "Every one who buys, takes or receives a lot, ticket or other device mentioned in subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 206(4) the person commits the offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(4) the person commits the offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(4) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 206(4) the punishment` `s 206(1) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST `s 206(1) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- (5) "Every sale ... by any lottery ... is void, and all property so sold ... is forfeited to Her Majesty"; (6) "Subsection (5) does not affect any right or title to property acquired by any bona fide purchaser for valuable consideration without notice"
#ASSERT `s 206(5) the sale, loan, gift, barter or exchange is void` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(5) the sale, loan, gift, barter or exchange is void` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(5) the property so sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(5) the property so sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(5) the property so sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(5) the property so sold, lent, given, bartered or exchanged is forfeited to Her Majesty` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(6) subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title to the property` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(6) subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title to the property` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(6) subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title to the property` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(6) subsection 206(5) does not affect the right or title to the property` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7) the section applies to a foreign lottery's advertisement, sale of tickets, or conducting
#ASSERT `s 206(7) section 206 applies to the thing done` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(7) section 206 applies to the thing done` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(7) section 206 applies to the thing done` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(7) section 206 applies to the thing done` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8) "This section does not apply to (a) the division by lot ... by joint tenants ...; (b) [Repealed]; or (c) bonds, debentures ... recallable by drawing of lots"
#ASSERT `s 206(8) section 206 does not apply to the thing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(8) section 206 does not apply to the thing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(8) section 206 does not apply to the thing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

